  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jinja waste RWS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at solving the municipal solid waste problem in Jinja, a town in Uganda approximately 81 km east of the capital, Kampala. It is located along the northern shores of Lake Victoria, near the source of the White Nile. Jinja Municipal Council must deal with waste and maintain cleanliness within the municipality. In 2011, the Council conducted an Environmental Impact Assessment for a proposed landfill and waste composting plant in a neighbouring village (Masese). This study indicates that only 45% of municipal waste is collected and disposed of due to resource limitations. The remaining 55% of the waste is dumped in the Nile, negatively impacting water quality and resulting in environmental degradation.The Jinja Municipal Council is searching for a private company or partner to help them collect and treat the waste and finance the investment by turning it into an income-generating activity through a Public Private Partnership tender. The Develop2Build (D2B) initiative aims to assist the Jinja Municipal Council by conducting various essential studies. These studies include enhancing the Environmental and Social Impact Assessment (ESIA) and conducting a pre-feasibility analysis focussing on problem analysis, waste composition and volumes. Additionally, the project aims to aid in preparing a tender for this particular undertaking.</narrative>
  </description>
